WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.190
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:42.460 --> 00:43.959
Morning...

3
00:43.960 --> 00:46.209
Huh? Leaving so early?

4
00:46.210 --> 00:48.880
Just remembered some work stuff.

5
00:50.250 --> 00:52.700
And here I was gonna make breakfast today.

6
00:53.260 --> 00:54.760
Remember to lock the door.

7
00:55.630 --> 00:56.970
Got it.

8
00:58.980 --> 01:00.080
Oh, right, tomorrow...

9
01:04.560 --> 01:06.320
I have a business trip.

10
01:09.610 --> 01:11.270
What happened that day three years ago...

11
01:12.840 --> 01:14.560
He's probably forgotten all about it.

12
01:15.900 --> 01:18.379
It's fine, don't worry about it.

13
01:18.380 --> 01:21.370
Kawakita-san from General Affairs is really great.

14
01:22.370 --> 01:24.120
Mizoguchi, set up a mixer for us!

15
01:24.910 --> 01:27.019
No way, ask her out yourself.

16
01:27.020 --> 01:29.180
Come on, I'll invite your crush too.

17
01:34.080 --> 01:36.790
With a reaction like that, there really is someone!

18
01:37.980 --> 01:39.080
Who is it?

19
01:41.480 --> 01:43.880
From Sales... Kobayashi.

20
01:44.800 --> 01:45.899
Seriously?

21
01:45.900 --> 01:48.289
Kobayashi, huh?

22
01:48.290 --> 01:50.369
Kobayashi...

23
01:50.370 --> 01:51.719
Huh?

24
01:51.720 --> 01:52.899
Does he have a girlfriend?

25
01:52.900 --> 01:55.420
No, he has a boyfriend.

26
01:56.280 --> 01:57.949
I'm only saying this because he's open about it.

27
01:57.950 --> 01:59.210
He's gay.

28
02:00.980 --> 02:02.080
Oh, I see...

29
02:02.960 --> 02:05.370
Either way, he seems super popular.

30
02:07.060 --> 02:08.620
Right...

31
02:12.260 --> 02:14.349
What about you, Kanda? Who would you ask out?

32
02:14.350 --> 02:16.299
Huh? Me?

33
02:16.300 --> 02:18.040
Well, I...

34
02:19.020 --> 02:20.470
I'm gonna hit the restroom.

35
02:22.980 --> 02:25.020
I wonder what Kanda's deal is.

36
02:29.480 --> 02:30.480
Makes you curious.

37
02:31.440 --> 02:33.330
Hey, are you okay?

38
02:37.070 --> 02:38.280
Are you drunk?

39
02:46.330 --> 02:47.280
Listen...

40
02:47.281 --> 02:48.420
Yeah?

41
02:50.920 --> 02:53.350
I'm actually gay.

42
02:57.320 --> 03:00.690
So sometimes I can't just play along with everyone.

43
03:04.560 --> 03:05.950
Sorry for keeping it from you.

44
03:09.900 --> 03:10.900
Oh, really?

45
03:14.220 --> 03:16.020
Why are you apologizing, though?

46
03:16.980 --> 03:18.630
There's nothing to be sorry about.

47
03:23.380 --> 03:24.380
Thanks.

48
03:25.080 --> 03:26.080
Yeah.

49
03:29.960 --> 03:31.560
Don't worry, though.

50
03:33.540 --> 03:35.289
You're not my type.

51
03:35.290 --> 03:38.210
Nothing's ever gonna happen between us.

52
03:40.420 --> 03:41.690
Well...

53
03:43.320 --> 03:45.319
He was just trying to make me feel comfortable, right?

54
03:45.320 --> 03:46.850
With what he just said.

55
03:47.840 --> 03:48.840
But even so...

56
03:53.620 --> 03:56.870
Did he have to shut it down that hard?

57
04:56.880 --> 04:59.340
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

58
05:01.760 --> 05:04.360
(Episode 3) True to his word, three years have passed since then.

59
05:04.900 --> 05:06.260
And between Ueno and me...

60
05:07.460 --> 05:08.840
nothing ever happened.

61
05:12.380 --> 05:15.440
Nothing happening at all is only natural, right?

62
05:17.080 --> 05:18.080
Oh.

63
05:20.433 --> 05:22.513
[Generic ad copy]

64
05:33.520 --> 05:34.520
Hey.

65
05:35.800 --> 05:37.000
Ueno, do you...

66
05:38.240 --> 05:41.310
like this TAKUMI guy from F:IVE?

67
05:45.550 --> 05:46.580
Why do you ask?

68
05:47.580 --> 05:51.510
Because your watch history is nothing but his videos.

69
05:55.540 --> 05:56.540
Not really.

70
06:00.190 --> 06:01.190
Just...

71
06:02.180 --> 06:04.000
I don't dislike him.

72
06:08.780 --> 06:12.149
Besides, the only reason Ueno is friends with me

73
06:12.150 --> 06:14.320
is because I'm not his type.

74
06:19.880 --> 06:23.320
(I'm TAKUMI from the vocal group F:IVE. Sharing lots of solo stuff and music content!)

75
06:28.340 --> 06:30.010
He liked so many of his posts.

76
06:31.020 --> 06:33.380
He's clearly super into him.

77
06:38.840 --> 06:40.040
Soft and cute.

78
06:41.020 --> 06:42.220
Puppy-dog type.

79
06:43.150 --> 06:44.900
Artistic vibe...

80
06:56.540 --> 06:58.320
Not like me at all.

81
07:00.080 --> 07:01.770
Not that I care, though.

82
07:12.400 --> 07:13.930
Wait, Kanda-san.

83
07:14.800 --> 07:16.329
Did you get a perm?

84
07:16.330 --> 07:17.549
Yeah.

85
07:17.550 --> 07:19.739
- It looks great on you. - Thanks.

86
07:19.740 --> 07:23.480
By the way, I heard Ueno-san is getting transferred.

87
07:34.740 --> 07:35.840
Thanks.

88
07:40.980 --> 07:42.850
How come I didn't hear about your transfer?

89
07:43.630 --> 07:44.790
Oh.

90
07:45.420 --> 07:46.549
Guess I didn't tell you.

91
07:46.550 --> 07:48.090
Man...

92
07:49.180 --> 07:51.020
That's cold, man.

93
07:53.140 --> 07:54.780
Why make a big deal out of it?

94
07:55.480 --> 07:56.930
It's not like I'm quitting.

95
07:58.580 --> 08:00.120
Why now, though?

96
08:02.340 --> 08:04.860
Heard someone's leaving due to illness.

97
08:05.540 --> 08:07.250
They've been looking for a replacement.

98
08:08.690 --> 08:10.750
Figured it'd suit me better than sales.

99
08:11.420 --> 08:12.420
I see.

100
08:19.440 --> 08:21.740
You're a natural at sales. Keep it up.

101
08:29.240 --> 08:30.240
Oh.

102
08:30.241 --> 08:31.420
By the way...

103
08:32.200 --> 08:33.590
Did you get a perm?

104
08:35.140 --> 08:36.720
Oh, yeah.

105
08:37.940 --> 08:38.940
I did.

106
08:41.600 --> 08:42.600
Looks good.

107
09:29.060 --> 09:30.060
Huh?

108
09:30.820 --> 09:32.030
Hair wax...

109
09:39.360 --> 09:40.360
Ah.

110
09:40.950 --> 09:42.090
It's at Ueno's place.

111
09:50.210 --> 09:54.480
If we're just friends, there's no need to style myself to his taste.

112
09:56.400 --> 10:00.950
Getting a perm and styling it every morning is such a hassle.

113
10:04.140 --> 10:05.140
Even so...

114
10:05.880 --> 10:07.700
Couldn't he at least notice me a little?

115
10:08.600 --> 10:09.770
Just me, as a person.

116
10:13.060 --> 10:14.400
Even if someone isn't your type,

117
10:15.180 --> 10:17.530
you can still fall for the person sitting next to you.

118
10:19.860 --> 10:21.659
Couldn't he...

119
10:21.660 --> 10:24.970
fall for me like that, too?

120
10:49.960 --> 10:50.960
I feel like...

121
10:52.060 --> 10:54.020
I just dreamed about Ueno.

122
11:04.440 --> 11:07.119
Welcome back. You look sleepy.

123
11:07.120 --> 11:08.380
I'm back.

124
11:08.880 --> 11:10.040
And good morning.

125
11:11.120 --> 11:13.060
How was the business trip to Sendai?

126
11:13.820 --> 11:16.379
I brought back zunda mochi as a souvenir.

127
11:16.380 --> 11:17.760
Thanks.

128
11:18.280 --> 11:19.859
Should I put it in the break room for everyone?

129
11:19.860 --> 11:21.130
Yeah, thanks.

130
11:25.010 --> 11:25.680
Not this bag, though.

131
11:25.681 --> 11:26.760
This is a personal gift.

132
11:27.660 --> 11:28.660
Gotcha.

133
11:49.120 --> 11:51.120
Can I come over tonight?

134
11:57.550 --> 11:58.550
Sorry.

135
11:58.551 --> 12:01.020
Don't come over until the end of the month.

136
12:04.090 --> 12:05.030
Huh?

137
12:05.031 --> 12:07.860
I have a friend staying over.

138
12:16.320 --> 12:17.650
A friend...

139
12:26.940 --> 12:29.079
Regarding supply volume, we'd like to maintain the status quo

140
12:29.080 --> 12:31.750
as we move forward with this project.

141
12:32.720 --> 12:34.670
Ethan, what do you think?

142
12:35.670 --> 12:36.420
Yeah that works.

143
12:36.854 --> 12:37.466
OK.

144
12:38.920 --> 12:40.499
Alright, please proceed with this plan.

145
12:40.500 --> 12:41.719
Yes, understood.

146
12:41.720 --> 12:43.130
Thank you very much.

147
12:46.090 --> 12:47.260
A friend...

148
12:48.460 --> 12:49.809
When you eat a chocolate cornet,

149
12:49.810 --> 12:52.329
you definitely have to start from the head.

150
12:52.330 --> 12:54.910
It's the golden ratio of bread and chocolate!

151
12:55.560 --> 12:57.520
Taking a big bite right here...

152
13:02.160 --> 13:03.400
A friend...

153
13:04.860 --> 13:05.860
is it?

154
13:14.600 --> 13:16.240
It happens from time to time.

155
13:17.080 --> 13:18.640
Periods when he won't let me come over.

156
13:19.980 --> 13:20.980
And yet...

157
13:21.630 --> 13:25.920
Whenever I go back later, I always pick up on little clues.

158
13:33.640 --> 13:36.650
Spotless floors.

159
13:37.560 --> 13:38.980
Freshly washed sheets.

160
13:39.860 --> 13:42.630
And incense burning, as if to cover up a trace of someone.

161
13:46.860 --> 13:52.120
Probably a friend with benefits.

162
13:57.040 --> 13:59.220
Kanda-san looks so deep in thought.

163
14:00.920 --> 14:02.020
He's so hot.

164
14:03.700 --> 14:06.090
The Lanau project seems really tough.

165
14:06.620 --> 14:08.190
He must be figuring out his next move.

166
14:10.430 --> 14:13.520
If he got a boyfriend, he'd take back my spare key.

167
14:19.360 --> 14:21.420
Might as well just give this to him at the office.

168
14:29.080 --> 14:31.030
Just got back from my Sendai trip.

169
14:38.330 --> 14:39.379
(Souvenir)

170
14:39.380 --> 14:40.460
Kanda-san.

171
14:41.260 --> 14:42.460
Do you have a minute?

172
14:43.080 --> 14:44.759
I'd love your advice on the internal pitch competition.

173
14:44.760 --> 14:46.220
Oh, sure.

174
14:47.760 --> 14:49.570
Let's see...

175
14:54.640 --> 14:55.850
Kobayashi.

176
14:56.800 --> 14:57.800
Yes?

177
15:00.100 --> 15:01.540
If you're free, how about tonight?

178
15:04.260 --> 15:05.260
Huh?

179
15:05.840 --> 15:06.840
Oh.

180
15:06.841 --> 15:08.761
Just the two of us might come off as harassment.

181
15:11.300 --> 15:12.300
What?

182
15:16.960 --> 15:18.869
You caught me off guard for a second there.

183
15:18.870 --> 15:21.210
Next time, just ask me out normally.

184
15:22.260 --> 15:23.459
How on earth did you ask him?

185
15:23.460 --> 15:26.049
Huh? Was it weird?

186
15:26.050 --> 15:28.920
Phrasing it like that is bad for my heart.

187
15:30.130 --> 15:32.850
- Excuse me, another draft beer. - Coming right up.

188
15:34.140 --> 15:35.110
Drinking fast tonight.

189
15:35.111 --> 15:36.560
In the mood to drink?

190
15:38.960 --> 15:39.960
Not really...

191
15:41.100 --> 15:43.560
I asked Kanda-san for some tips on the internal competition.

192
15:44.220 --> 15:45.359
It's that time of year already, huh?

193
15:45.360 --> 15:48.089
Lucky for me, we have a former champion right here.

194
15:48.090 --> 15:50.489
- True. - Excuse me, here's your draft beer.

195
15:50.490 --> 15:51.739
Thanks.

196
15:51.740 --> 15:52.740
Sorry, actually...

197
15:56.080 --> 15:57.080
There's something I...

198
15:57.700 --> 15:59.140
wanted to ask you, too, Kobayashi.

199
16:00.180 --> 16:01.180
What's up?

200
16:06.920 --> 16:10.650
Is it possible to see a straight friend as a romantic interest?

201
16:14.380 --> 16:15.380
Oh.

202
16:16.780 --> 16:17.890
It's not impossible.

203
16:18.850 --> 16:19.949
I've dated a straight guy before.

204
16:19.950 --> 16:20.930
Wait, seriously?

205
16:20.931 --> 16:23.050
How did that even happen?

206
16:25.000 --> 16:26.000
Well...

207
16:26.001 --> 16:27.319
Way too close!

208
16:27.320 --> 16:28.580
Back up a little.

209
16:29.780 --> 16:32.280
- Oh... - My bad...

210
16:35.620 --> 16:36.819
Back when I was a student...

211
16:36.820 --> 16:41.310
It started out as a joke, but then he suddenly said he wanted to try it with a guy.

212
16:42.500 --> 16:43.660
And one thing led to another.

213
16:44.630 --> 16:45.710
Led to what?

214
16:48.300 --> 16:49.690
You know...

215
16:52.120 --> 16:54.420
Oh, don't mind me. Go right ahead.

216
16:57.346 --> 16:58.715
After we slept together,

217
16:58.930 --> 17:00.730
it just naturally turned into a relationship.

218
17:07.400 --> 17:08.500
So you're saying...

219
17:09.360 --> 17:12.540
he developed feelings for you after sleeping together?

220
17:14.100 --> 17:15.100
I mean,

221
17:15.720 --> 17:20.090
if you're gonna date a straight guy, isn't sleeping together the first real hurdle?

222
17:25.420 --> 17:29.479
He didn't think he could do it, but it turned out he could.

223
17:29.480 --> 17:33.230
So we figured we'd give dating a shot.

224
17:38.560 --> 17:39.860
Sleeping together, huh...

225
17:40.940 --> 17:41.940
Wait, what?

226
17:42.900 --> 17:44.950
So that really is what it all comes down to...

227
17:52.000 --> 17:53.740
What on earth is he talking about?

228
17:54.700 --> 17:55.820
What's up with Kanda?

229
18:00.040 --> 18:01.580
Just leave him be.

230
18:05.460 --> 18:07.539
- Excuse me! - Yes, coming right up!

231
18:07.540 --> 18:09.420
- I'll take another one. - Sure thing.

232
18:16.080 --> 18:17.280
Morning.

233
18:18.320 --> 18:19.320
Good morning.

234
18:19.480 --> 18:20.480
Morning.

235
18:22.220 --> 18:24.060
Oh, morning.

236
18:26.240 --> 18:27.780
I'm here for the edamame mochi.

237
18:32.110 --> 18:33.679
Again?

238
18:33.680 --> 18:36.070
(Advance Expense Settlement Form - Entertainment Expenses.)

239
18:37.990 --> 18:40.450
(Advance Expense Summary Sheet - Settled by: Kanda Eito.)

240
18:44.960 --> 18:46.360
Oh, there's only one left.

241
18:47.060 --> 18:48.060
Lucky you.

242
18:49.660 --> 18:51.320
I'll take this as your apology.

243
18:52.220 --> 18:53.220
Apology for what?

244
18:55.420 --> 18:57.070
Don't talk to Kobayashi about romance

245
18:58.300 --> 19:01.520
right in front of me.

246
19:06.850 --> 19:08.299
Wait, you still have feelings for him?

247
19:08.300 --> 19:10.440
Hold on, but Kobayashi is...

248
19:10.980 --> 19:11.980
I know.

249
19:12.700 --> 19:13.700
I've already given up.

250
19:14.540 --> 19:16.499
But human feelings don't work like that.

251
19:16.500 --> 19:19.569
You can't just go, "Oh, I see, guess I'll stop liking him then,"

252
19:19.570 --> 19:22.410
and magically move on.

253
19:23.950 --> 19:24.950
Fair point...

254
19:26.300 --> 19:28.679
Wait, wasn't that three years ago, though?

255
19:28.680 --> 19:30.080
Yeah.

256
19:33.420 --> 19:34.420
Seriously...

257
19:34.960 --> 19:37.340
Even I think I'm pathetic.

258
19:38.000 --> 19:39.000
Jeez.

259
19:39.560 --> 19:40.680
I'm really sorry about that.

260
19:41.920 --> 19:43.520
Why don't you just confess to him, then?

261
19:44.010 --> 19:45.969
Just walk right into a rejection?

262
19:45.970 --> 19:47.949
At least it'd give you some closure.

263
19:47.950 --> 19:49.960
Maybe it would for me,

264
19:51.060 --> 19:52.839
but that'd just put Kobayashi in an awkward spot.

265
19:52.840 --> 19:55.670
Getting confessed to by someone who knows he's gay.

266
19:58.900 --> 19:59.900
Yeah, I guess.

267
20:04.160 --> 20:05.700
That sounds rough.

268
20:07.040 --> 20:08.549
It is rough!

269
20:08.550 --> 20:09.779
Yeah.

270
20:09.780 --> 20:11.920
- What am I supposed to do?! - Ow!

271
20:12.460 --> 20:13.699
How should I know?

272
20:13.700 --> 20:15.039
Stop hitting me, that hurts!

273
20:15.040 --> 20:19.169
- Do you get it now? It's complicated! - I'm really sorry, I apologize!

274
20:19.170 --> 20:21.439
So just hear me out...

275
20:21.440 --> 20:25.279
- Calm down, sit, and eat your mochi. - Eating this isn't gonna calm me down!

276
20:25.280 --> 20:28.140
Why not? I bought that for you guys!

277
21:55.730 --> 21:59.150
It's already expired!

278
22:07.820 --> 22:10.360
Is your friend still at your place?

279
22:19.320 --> 22:20.520
Seriously...

280
22:21.250 --> 22:23.940
What am I even trying to do?

281
22:31.180 --> 22:34.390
(Kanda Satoshi: Can I count on your help again this month?)

282
23:00.649 --> 23:02.364
(Kanda Eito: Is your friend still at your place?)

283
23:02.408 --> 23:04.596
(Kanda Eito: I'm back from my business trip to Sendai.)

284
23:24.320 --> 23:25.960
I need to find something to keep me busy.

285
23:28.840 --> 23:31.470
As long as I can live a fulfilling life on my own,

286
23:32.460 --> 23:34.470
if I can just manage that,

287
23:37.200 --> 23:41.040
there won't be any room for feelings like love to sneak in.

288
23:44.880 --> 23:47.496
(Next Episode Preview) Someone asked me to start a business with them.

289
23:47.520 --> 23:49.820
Just seeing your face is enough for me. I'm heading back.

290
23:50.400 --> 23:53.960
Truth is, someone I met on a dating app came over.

291
23:54.620 --> 23:55.720
What is this feeling?

292
23:56.240 --> 23:59.310
I really just want Ueno to spoil me right now.
